# Git workflow

## Branches — hard rules

- **NEVER touch `main`.** Do not push to it, open PRs into it, merge into it, rebase onto it for delivery, or cherry-pick “onto main”. Production CD fires from `main`; treating it as a working base is a mistake.
- **Deployable / integration branch is `feat/pos-books-web`.** All feature PRs for potta-web must target `feat/pos-books-web` (staging CD). Open work from that branch: `git checkout -b feat/<topic> origin/feat/pos-books-web`.
- Feature work lives on `feat/<topic>` branches. Example: POS + Books slimming and payment-methods UX land via PRs into `feat/pos-books-web`.

## Commits / push

- Only commit or push when the user asks. Push the current branch with `git push origin HEAD`; never force-push `main`, `staging`, or `feat/pos-books-web` unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Before committing: `npm run typecheck` and `npm run lint` on the files you changed.
- Never commit `.env*` files except `.env.example`.

## Auth backend note (cross-repo)

- For **instanvi-auth-starter**, the deployable branch is `dev` (not `main`).
